---
import Base from '../layouts/MiseBase.astro';
import Hero from '../components/mise/Hero.astro';
import Step from '../components/mise/Step.astro';
import Shot from '../components/mise/Shot.astro';
import Faq from '../components/mise/Faq.astro';
import Footer from '../components/mise/Footer.astro';
import { URLS } from '../mise/config.js';

const faq = [
  {
    q: 'Which formats?',
    a: '<code>wav</code> <code>aif</code> <code>flac</code> <code>mp3</code> <code>m4a</code> <code>aac</code> <code>ogg</code> <code>caf</code>. Anything Core Audio reads, Mise reads.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What does it need?',
    a: 'macOS 26 on the Mac. iOS 26 on iPhone and iPad. The same Apple Account signed in on each, and a Dropbox if you want one library on all of them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need Dropbox?',
    a: 'Not on one device: open Mise, record, bring in files, play. To have the same library on your Mac, iPhone and iPad, it has to be a folder in your Dropbox. That is the one shared home in this version.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Where does my library live?',
    a: 'In a folder of your Dropbox, as ordinary files, or on the device if you keep it to one. Mise keeps its index in a <code>.mise</code> folder next to them. There is no Mise account.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What about iCloud Drive?',
    a: 'Not in this version. Mise does not read or keep a library in iCloud Drive. Your Apple Account is used only to carry what you do — stars, crates, marks, what each sound is — between your own devices, in its private database.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Does the Mac have to stay on?',
    a: 'No. Each sound is analyzed once, by whichever device gets to it first, and every device then carries the result. A phone with no Mac behind it analyzes its own sounds.',
  },
];

const families = ['kicks', 'snares', 'claps', 'hats & shakers', 'cymbals', 'toms', 'percussion', '808 & bass', 'keys', 'leads & plucks', 'stabs & chords', 'pads & texture', 'vocals', 'fx & sweeps', 'noise & vinyl', 'foley'];
---

<Base>
  <Hero />

  <main>
    <!-- 01 Connect -->
    <Step
      id="connect"
      n="01"
      name="Connect"
      tone="limao"
      headline="Every sound you own, in one list."
      bullets={[
        'Dropbox, Voice Memos, Ableton projects, Rekordbox, any folder on your Mac.',
        'Dropbox sounds are listed from Dropbox&rsquo;s own index. Nothing downloads until you press play.',
        'Every sound gets an id off its own bytes, so the same sample under three names is known as one sound.',
        'Every sound is analyzed once. The phone carries the results, not the files.',
      ]}
    >
      <Fragment slot="body">
        <p>Samples end up everywhere: a Dropbox from an old collaborator, a folder of voice memos, four years of Ableton projects with bounces inside them. Mise reads them where they are and brings scattered audio into one library, without moving anything you did not ask it to move.</p>
      </Fragment>
      <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-dropbox.png" kind="mac" alt="A Dropbox folder listed as a source in Mise on Mac, every sound visible before any of it has downloaded." caption="mac-dropbox.png" />
      <div class="pair">
        <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-library.png" kind="mac" alt="The Mise library on Mac, sounds from several sources in one list." caption="mac-library.png" />
        <Shot src="/mise/shots/ipad-docked.png" kind="ipad" alt="Mise on iPad: the tape with the sous’s page open — the family it chose, the words it found, the nearest sounds." caption="ipad-docked.png" />
      </div>
    </Step>

    <!-- 02 Prep -->
    <Step
      id="prep"
      n="02"
      name="Prep"
      tone="acai"
      flip
      headline="Find the good ones. Say what you mean."
      bullets={[
        'Search by sound or by name. A typed sentence and a file are compared in the same space.',
        'Surface the forgotten: never played, a random deal, sounds like this one.',
        'Favorite, tag, cue and mark, trim, normalize. Organize into crates.',
        'Audition as loops, keys, slices or kits before you commit to anything.',
        'Sixteen families, sorted by the sous. Your own named folders teach it your vocabulary.',
      ]}
    >
      <Fragment slot="body">
        <p>A CLAP model turns every sound and every typed sentence into 512 numbers in one space. So <strong>“a dusty vinyl kick”</strong> finds files called <strong>1234.wav</strong>, and a sound you like finds its siblings across every source.</p>
        <p class="families" aria-label="The sixteen families">
          {families.map((f) => <span class="family">{f}</span>)}
        </p>
      </Fragment>
      <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-search-by-sound.png" kind="mac" alt="Search by sound on Mac: a typed sentence at the top, the closest sounds ranked beneath it." caption="mac-search-by-sound.png" />
      <div class="pair">
        <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-ear.png" kind="mac" alt="The sous on Mac: sounds sorted into families, with a folder teaching it a new word." caption="mac-ear.png" />
        <div class="pair pair--phones">
          <Shot src="/mise/shots/ios-library.png" kind="phone" alt="The library on iPhone with the chip row filtering to one family." caption="ios-library.png" />
          <Shot src="/mise/shots/ios-crates.png" kind="phone" alt="Crates on iPhone: named collections of sounds, ready for a project." caption="ios-crates.png" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </Step>

    <!-- 03 Cook -->
    <Step
      id="cook"
      n="03"
      name="Cook"
      tone="maracuja"
      headline="Shape it. Send it anywhere."
      bullets={[
        'Pitch as tape or keep the pitch. Reverse, stretch, saturate.',
        'Resample the whole thing, the loop, a slice at your marks, or 8 and 16 even slices.',
        'Every new sound keeps its lineage back to the parent.',
        'Cut ten seconds of any sound into sixteen pads, by stem.',
        'Keep your Rekordbox playlists as crates, and your crates as playlists.',
        'Drag into Ableton or Logic as the file. Kits for OP-XY and crates for MPC, in testing.',
        'Hand a sound to another device and it is there.',
      ]}
    >
      <Fragment slot="body">
        <p>The tape is where a sound becomes yours. Pull it down an octave, stretch it over a bar, drive it a little. Print what you hear as a new sound in the library, and the library remembers where it came from.</p>
      </Fragment>
      <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-tape.png" kind="mac" alt="The tape as a drawer on the Mac, with the sous’s page open under it." caption="mac-tape.png" />
      <div class="pair">
        <Shot src="/mise/shots/mac-resample.png" kind="mac" alt="Search by sound on the Mac: every kick in a library of 145,000, closest first, with how far the match drops off." caption="mac-resample.png" />
        <div class="pair pair--phones">
          <Shot src="/mise/shots/ios-tape.png" kind="phone" alt="The tape on iPhone, one thumb on the pitch." caption="ios-tape.png" />
          <Shot src="/mise/shots/ios-record.png" kind="phone" alt="Recording on iPhone: a level meter, the location, the threshold armed." caption="ios-record.png" />
        </div>
      </div>
    </Step>

    <!-- Record + Private -->
    <section class="two section">
      <div class="wrap two__grid">
        <div class="two__col">
          <p class="label" style="color: var(--pimenta)">Record</p>
          <h2 class="h3">Catch it while it is happening.</h2>
          <p class="body">
            Field recordings keep their location. On the Mac, record whatever any app is playing: a browser tab, a synth, a call. Set a threshold and recording starts on the first sound, so the take begins where the sound does.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="two__col">
          <p class="label label--dim">Private by design</p>
          <h2 class="h3">Your sounds stay yours.</h2>
          <p class="body">
            The models that analyze and sort run on the device. Your library is a folder in your own Dropbox; what you do to a sound travels between your devices through your own Apple Account. There is no account to make and no server of ours.
          </p>
          <ul class="two__facts mono">
            <li>on-device models</li>
            <li>your Dropbox</li>
            <li>no account</li>
            <li>no server</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <Faq items={faq} />

    <!-- Closing CTA -->
    <section class="close section">
      <div class="wrap close__grid">
        <h2 class="h2">One place for all of it.</h2>
        <div class="close__cta">
          <a class="btn btn--limao" href={URLS.invite}>Ask for an invite</a>
          <a class="btn btn--ghost" href={URLS.support}>Support</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .families {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .family {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    color: var(--acai-text);
    background: var(--wash);
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    border-radius: 999px;
    padding: 0.3em 0.75em;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .two__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
  .two__col { display: grid; gap: 1.25rem; align-content: start; }
  .two__facts {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.5rem 1.25rem;
    color: var(--faint);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
  }
  .two__facts li::before {
    content: '';
    display: inline-block;
    width: 0.4rem;
    height: 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 999px;
    background: var(--limao);
    margin-right: 0.5rem;
    transform: translateY(-0.05em);
  }
  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .two__grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }

  .close__grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2rem;
    justify-items: start;
  }
  .close__cta {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.75rem;
  }
</style>
